- `action(n14, "Start homework assignment")`: Missing outgoing precedence edge, breaking the workflow cycle described in "another homework assignment will be given."
- `action(n7, "Request exception again")`: Missing outgoing precedence edge, creating a dead end despite the source implying a retry loop for unapproved exceptions.
- `precedence(n25, n27)` & `end(e2)`: Incorrectly routes exam failures directly to process termination instead of looping back to exam registration, contradicting "If the exam is failed, another sign-up for the exam is required."
- `defines(v1, "Is an exception needed for course registration", {})`, `defines(v3, "Is this the last homework", {})`, `defines(v4, "Did the exam pass", {})`: Declared with empty ranges `{}`, failing to represent the binary decision options (Yes/No, Last/Not last, Pass/Fail) explicitly stated in the source.
- `defines(v2, "Is the exception approved", {"Continue"})` and `guard(b2, c1, v2 = 'Continue')`: The range value "Continue" and corresponding guard condition inaccurately model an approval status decision; they should reflect approval outcomes (e.g., Approved/Denied) rather than a procedural flow descriptor, misaligning with "After the exception is approved."

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n14` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n7` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n14,"Start homework assignment"); action(n7,"Request exception again")
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `['Continue']`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v4` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v2 = 'Continue'` on `b2 -> c1` uses undefined variable `v2`. | DSL: guard(b2,c1,"v2 = 'Continue'")
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n3` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n7` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n13` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n15` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n23` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n24` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S5] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: n13, n14, n7 | DSL: action(n13,"Assign another homework"); action(n14,"Start homework assignment"); action(n7,"Request exception again")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v2 = 'Continue'` on `b2 -> c1` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b2,c1,"v2 = 'Continue'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b2` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range.
